  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "A signed agreement's traceable trail: calm blue working surfaces, a continuous loop brand, deliberate alignment and clear ownership. This is an operating tool for Brightloop's staff and customers. Information, permissions and the next honest action lead every surface. The category's generic KPI dashboard and a decorative finance terminal are anti-references.",
    "overview": "A signed agreement's traceable trail: calm blue working surfaces, a continuous loop brand, deliberate alignment and clear ownership. This is an operating tool for Brightloop's staff and customers. Information, permissions and the next honest action lead every surface. The category's generic KPI dashboard and a decorative finance terminal are anti-references.\n\nThe brief supplies English software operations and local resilience; INR and Asia/Kolkata are implementation policy, not a claimed market study. The main usage scene is daily desktop work with a narrow-screen record-check path. Register is product throughout. No Japan-market scope is established.\n\nThe root task authorizes a new product, with no incumbent visual identity. The task-derived direction is the agreement trail; blue, white and precise type carry forward into later gates. One signature, quiet surroundings. Do not build empty navigation for future gates.\n\nToken ownership: this file defines the visual contract; `src/styles.css` maps the named values one-to-one to `--color-*` custom properties. No framework adapter or generated theme exists. Shared components consume these variables. Change both sources together and use the strict premium audit plus browser screenshots to inspect drift.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "One continuous agreement trail",
      "Clear role and ownership",
      "Flat working surfaces",
      "No decorative financial data"
    ],
    "rules": [],
    "dos": [
      "Do show who can act and what happened, using persisted data.",
      "Do keep create/read/search feedback and focus consistent across sibling staff/customer lists."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't fill future navigation with dead buttons or synthetic operational claims.",
      "Don't add decoration that obscures identity, permission or financial information."
    ]
  }
}
